message: "If you use Recall Guard, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Recall Guard"
version: 0.5.0
date-released: 2026-10-30
license: MIT
authors:
  - family-names: Ciepluch
    given-names: Marius
repository-code: "https://github.com/norandom/memguard_alpha"
url: "https://github.com/norandom/memguard_alpha/releases/tag/v0.5.0"
abstract: >-
  Recall Guard is a Python package for per-prompt contamination scoring of LLM
  outputs, with harness workflows for model comparison and a single-model
  thresholded cmmd backtest.
references:
  - type: article
    title: "Computational Global Macro with AI for Risk and Portfolio Management"
    authors:
      - family-names: Ciepluch
        given-names: Marius
    year: 2026
    month: 7
    url: "https://papers.ssrn.com/sol3/papers.cfm?abstract_id=7231358"
    notes: >-
      SSRN working paper, abstract 7231358. Applies the Recall Guard
      Memorization Confidence Score as the point-in-time discount in an
      AI-inferred macro-factor overlay.
